    "blurb": "The project presents up-to-date, searchable editions of   the “Amarna letters,” the diplomatic correspondence in Akkadian   cuneiform dating to the mid-14th century BC and found at Tell el-Amarna (ancient Akhetaten) in Egypt.  By Jacob Lauinger (Johns Hopkins University) and Tyler Yoder (Culver Academies) and supported by a Catalyst Award from Johns Hopkins University",
